johnny silverhand is the zac de la rocha  of the cyberpunk universe  a musician with a radical  anti-establishment message  johnny's a disgruntled veteran of the  1990s central american conflict an  anarchist  and most importantly the first rocker  boy here's the origins and rise to fame  of one of cyberpunk's most prolific  characters  a rocker boy is a class wholly unique to  creator mike pondsmith cyberpunk  universe  rocker boys and gals are charismatic  public figures  who speak up against the powers that be  they usually come in the form of  musicians like johnny silverhand but  they don't have to shred the guitar or  play an instrument to be considered a  rocker boy  according to pondsmith himself to be a  rocker boy you just need to be able to  eloquently  stick it to the man and convince your  buds to stick it to the man with you  man but rock boy doesn't have to be a  musician a rocker boy  can be anyone who's a orator of the  people  anybody who can talk to others  and convince them by the power of words  music sometimes art and so forth  although johnny silverhand is a 100 year  old rock legend in cyberpunk 2077 his  story begins in the 1990s during the  central american conflict a bloody  struggle launched by the united states  war machine to squash communism  unsurprisingly the united states had  ulterior motives there were important  resources at play that the united states  government wanted a piece of while the  us did a good job of keeping this a  secret from the general population  soldiers began to uncover the  government's underhanded intentions  many enlisted soldiers broken and  battered at this point deserted and  returned to the united states  among these deserters was one robert  john under  after losing an arm he returned to night  city with a red-hot rebellious spark  in his eyes after getting fitted with a  new arasaka design cybernetic arm he  changed his name  to johnny silverhand and formed a band  called samurai  the group consisted of carrie eurodyne  denny bes  isis formerly known as nancy and henry  you know  good old henry samurai's music was a  global phenomenon  the world knew who johnny silverhand was  and they heard his messages of rebellion  and revolution  loud and clear samurai criticized  government world leaders  and of course the mega corporations that  ruled the world  more importantly samurai's music lit a  fire under the general public  everyday folks were picking up  instruments and getting their message  out there and so  the rocker boy was born unfortunately  samurai came to an abrupt end when nancy  pushed her abusive boyfriend out of a  window and  killed him i say good for nancy but the  united states justice system  seemed to disagree and put her behind  bars shortly after samurai separated  johnny silverham kicked off his solo  career his first solo release was titled  sins of your brothers  if his work with samurai consisted of  vague lessons in rebellion sins of your  brothers overtly called out the  injustices of the central american  conflict  johnny's first solo album proved to be a  massive hit  not only did it sell like crazy but it  changed the world's perception of the  central american conflict and shined a  light on the united states imperialistic  practices  things were going well for johnny his  fame was on the rise and he started  seeing a woman named alteria cunningham  or alt for short alt an incredibly  talented netrunner created a program  called soulkiller that essentially rips  a netrunner's mind from their skull and  makes a copy of it inside a mainframe  the body  still alive is left to decay the good  times sputtered to a halt when arasaka  thugs kidnapped all to get a hold of her  soul killer program  johnny in a fit of rage devised a plan  to rescue alt from the arasaka building  with the help of thompson a famous  journalist with a distaste for mega  corpse  it's important to note that at this  point johnny hates  arasaka he already did to some extent  but now things are  personal i imagine he'll make his hatred  of arasaka  very clear in cyberpunk 2077.  i'm sure he also hates that shiny metal  arasaka arm he's rocking  with the help of his former bandmates  johnny silverhand puts on a free show  near the arasaka building to hopefully  incite a riot then johnny would lead an  assault on arasaka to save  alt just like when rage against the  machine performed at the democratic  national convention in 2000 a riot  erupted outside of the arasaka building  after samurai played a song titled chip  and in  fun fact swedish hardcore band refused  did an official rendition of this song  which you can listen to right now as  well as a few other samurai songs  johnny's crew with a crowd of 6 000  broke into arasaka headquarters  sadly they were too late alt was dead  and her mind was trapped in a mainframe  this particular section comes from a  story titled never fade away in the  cyberpunk 2020 rulebook we will most  likely visit this event in another video  but if you want a more in-depth look at  this key moment in johnny's life we  recommend reading the full story  after that johnny disappeared there were  rumors that the indomitable cyborg adam  smasher put a bullet in johnny but his  remains were never  found of course this isn't the last time  we'll hear from johnny silverhand  as his electronic ghost seems to play a  significant role in cyberpunk 2077  played by the illustrious keanu reeves  cyberpunk  there's a brief overview of johnny  silverhand's life and legacy there's a  lot more to this story but we'll have to  wait until november to find out more  in the meantime if there's a cyberpunk  topic you'd like to see us cover leave  it in the comment sections below and  make sure to tune in next week as  jean-luc breaks down  johnny's arch nemesis arasaka and with  that we'll see you next time samurai  backing down
 

